    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d340">

                <pb facs="0488" n="400" sameAs="frus:frus1892/pg400"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr.
                            Strobel.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-09-05"><hi rendition="#italic">September 5,
                        1887</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 218.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring you to No. 217 of the 2d instant,
                    concerning the case of Rev. Mr. Doane, the American missionary arrested by the
                    authorities of the Philippine Islands, I now transmit additional information
                    contained in a further letter of Mr. Smith of the American Board of
                    Commissioners for Foreign Missions, of which you will make the proper use.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. F. Bayard.</hi></signed></closer>





